From bcc3fd26d516e2076c905113b99888f1746cb4d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arttttt <artem-bambalov@yandex.ru>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 05:34:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] tinyalsa: tinyplay: return the PCM format, not a bool

signed_pcm_bits_to_format() was declared bool, so it worked by accident
for 16-bit (PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE, 0) and mapped every other width to
true, PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE: an 8- or 24-bit WAV was opened as S32_LE and
played as noise. Taken from upstream tinyalsa f5368cd ("tinyplay: fix
playback of 24-bit and 8-bit pcm"), which AOSP's tinyalsa_new predates.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 utils/tinyplay.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/utils/tinyplay.c b/utils/tinyplay.c
index 96d0f60..1648418 100644
--- a/utils/tinyplay.c
+++ b/utils/tinyplay.c
@@ -111,7 +111,7 @@ static bool is_wave_file(const char *filetype)
     return filetype != NULL && strcmp(filetype, "wav") == 0;
 }
 
-static bool signed_pcm_bits_to_format(int bits)
+static enum pcm_format signed_pcm_bits_to_format(int bits)
 {
     switch (bits) {
     case 8:
-- 
2.56.0

